# Peer dependencies are provided by the dev workspace root, which installs
# @deepseek-ai/dsh at one exact version — the read-only checkout's, currently
# 0.2.1-rc.3 (npm's `next`, deliberately ahead of the installed desktop runtime).
# Auto-installing peers here would give this package its own floating copies (npm
# picks the highest matching prerelease, i.e. the `next` tag) and a second `zod`
# instance, which breaks type identity for `defineDomain` — see
# .agents/notes/implemented/2026-10-24-runtime-alignment-021.md, and for why the
# version follows the checkout .agents/notes/implemented/2026-10-24-runtime-alignment-rc3.md
# Pinning the peers as exact devDependencies is not an alternative: measured, it
# installs a second copy of every DSH package here — see
# .agents/notes/implemented/2026-10-24-peer-resolution-is-a-dev-workspace-fact.md
legacy-peer-deps=true
